  "mechanismSummary": "Imidazole attacks the silicon of tert-butyldimethylsilyl chloride and displaces chloride, giving an N-silylimidazolium ion, a much more reactive silylating agent than TBSCl itself. The primary OH of butane-1,3-diol attacks silicon and imidazole leaves again; a second imidazole removes the proton. The bulky TBS group goes on the less hindered primary OH first. TBS ethers survive base, organometallics, oxidation and mild acid, and come off with fluoride. Substitution at silicon is drawn here as one step; silicon can hold five groups for a moment, as the fluoride reaction shows.",
